{:edb/db-before-t 804 :edb/db-after-t 805 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534117 50 #inst "2026-10-06T03:16:24.630Z" 13194139534117 true] [17592186059604 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277727 13194139534117 true] [17592186059605 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277734 13194139534117 true] [17592186059606 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277720 13194139534117 true] [17592186060141 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534117 true] [17592186060141 1100 "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}?$\n\n- $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$\n- $\\frac{10\\pi }{3}$\n- $-\\frac{8\\pi }{3}$" 13194139534117 true] [17592186060141 1100 "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $θ =-\\frac{2π}{3}$?\n\n1. $\\frac{4π}{3}$\n2. $\\frac{10π}{3}$\n3. $-\\frac{8π}{3}$" 13194139534117 false] [17592186060141 1145 "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of $2\\pi :$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of $2\\pi $ to $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$:\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\cdot (2\\pi )=\\frac{10\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than $\\frac{10\\pi }{3}.$ So, we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of $2\\pi $ from $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$:\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-2\\pi =-\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\,✓$\n\n- $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-2\\cdot (2\\pi )=-\\frac{14\\pi }{3}$\n\nOf the given angles, all three are coterminal with $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I, II, and III." 13194139534117 true] [17592186060191 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534117 true] [17592186060191 1100 "The angle $\\theta =-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" 13194139534117 true] [17592186060191 1100 "The angle $θ =-\\frac{9π}{4}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" 13194139534117 false] [17592186060191 1145 "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ by *adding* integer multiples of $2\\pi $ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n- $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$\n\n- $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+2\\cdot (2\\pi )=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ is coterminal with $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/assets/891959642b0d055d852329c59be7541179dd5ae0c4182c2bec533261ce3a700d.png)\n\nWe see that $\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$ lies in quadrant IV. Therefore, $-\\frac{9\\pi }{4}$ also lies in this quadrant." 13194139534117 true] [17592186277720 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277721 13194139534117 true] [17592186277720 1089 "q-124707" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277720 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534117 true] [17592186277720 1100 "The angle $\\theta =-{530}^{∘}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277720 1113 #uuid "eaa1873e-b871-5487-ad2a-55300889eb98" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277720 1145 "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{530}^{∘}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$\n\n- $-{530}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}=-170$\n\n- $-{530}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={190}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${190}^{∘}$ is coterminal with $-{530}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977500/assets/1e741939f538fc5dfba9b5ff6f3b4ce0e68c5ebd746dfae533d3209c0c29feba.png)\n\nWe see that ${190}^{∘}$ lies in quadrant III. Therefore, $-{530}^{∘}$ also lies in this quadrant." 13194139534117 true] [17592186277721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277722 13194139534117 true] [17592186277721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277723 13194139534117 true] [17592186277721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277724 13194139534117 true] [17592186277721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277725 13194139534117 true] [17592186277721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277726 13194139534117 true] [17592186277721 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534117 true] [17592186277721 1041 "selection" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277721 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277723 13194139534117 true] [17592186277721 1110 #uuid "3bcc09e5-bdca-52ca-a12b-94e93877a51f" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277722 1034 "II" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277722 1111 #uuid "56e38090-95df-5db7-8495-6bea995248d8" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277723 1034 "III" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277723 1111 #uuid "f996bccc-b3d3-5796-bcf0-cb628bc10d4c" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277724 1034 "IV" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277724 1111 #uuid "66da0f38-31fa-5f51-8bd1-0b5e6a0fe3b1" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277725 1034 "Between quadrants II and III" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277725 1111 #uuid "aee4d362-b9eb-5fb6-99a1-bd156728dc9b" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277726 1034 "I" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277726 1111 #uuid "30e87dee-e647-52cd-9da8-56fc054e7e52" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277727 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277728 13194139534117 true] [17592186277727 1089 "q-22979" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277727 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534117 true] [17592186277727 1100 "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-{95}^{∘}?$\n\n- ${625}^{∘}$\n- ${160}^{∘}$\n- $-{455}^{∘}$" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277727 1113 #uuid "aba695cd-659a-5af1-80a1-f8970be8eb8b" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277727 1145 "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}:$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ to $-{95}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={265}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={625}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than ${625}^{∘}.$ So we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ from $-{95}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{455}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only ${625}^{∘}$ and $-{455}^{∘}$ are coterminal with $-{95}^{∘}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only." 13194139534117 true] [17592186277728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277729 13194139534117 true] [17592186277728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277730 13194139534117 true] [17592186277728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277731 13194139534117 true] [17592186277728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277732 13194139534117 true] [17592186277728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277733 13194139534117 true] [17592186277728 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534117 true] [17592186277728 1041 "selection" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277728 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277730 13194139534117 true] [17592186277728 1110 #uuid "c8cd84e6-a4ce-5bbc-a7ae-323b44b80f19" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277729 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277729 1111 #uuid "4d3afba9-fd91-5793-aee8-3718f16f14f2" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277730 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277730 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277730 1111 #uuid "23c60861-0323-5edb-acec-b21d51321b99" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277731 1034 "I only" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277731 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277731 1111 #uuid "0fd7ba99-a50a-59f8-be62-1376c3f6f614" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277732 1034 "III only" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277732 1111 #uuid "afc08a3c-efbb-5077-adfa-ca8afaf5cbf6" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277733 1034 "II only" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277733 1111 #uuid "de4cd345-bf42-56df-a44e-cc43b61b90ae" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277734 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277735 13194139534117 true] [17592186277734 1089 "q-22984" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277734 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534117 true] [17592186277734 1100 "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =2\\pi $\n\n- $4\\pi $\n- $5\\pi $\n- $-2\\pi $" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277734 1113 #uuid "72a396d7-e8cf-5458-9d0a-c10ca03427ce" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277734 1145 "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of $2\\pi :$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of $2\\pi $ to $2\\pi $:\n\n- $2\\pi +2\\pi =4\\pi \\,✓$\n\n- $2\\pi +2\\cdot (2\\pi )=6\\pi $\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than $6\\pi .$ So, we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of $2\\pi $ from $2\\pi $:\n\n- $2\\pi -2\\pi =0$\n\n- $2\\pi -2\\cdot (2\\pi )=-2\\pi \\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only $4\\pi $ and $-2\\pi $ are coterminal with $2\\pi .$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only." 13194139534117 true] [17592186277735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277736 13194139534117 true] [17592186277735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277737 13194139534117 true] [17592186277735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277738 13194139534117 true] [17592186277735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277739 13194139534117 true] [17592186277735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277740 13194139534117 true] [17592186277735 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534117 true] [17592186277735 1041 "selection" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277735 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277737 13194139534117 true] [17592186277735 1110 #uuid "f379d197-7992-501b-88af-92f31e188315" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277736 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534117 true] [17592186277736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534117 true] [17592186277736 1111 #uuid "f3700d87-3443-5005-9334-e439aa751883" 131941395